# How to cite ZXV. GitHub shows this as "Cite this repository".
# The DOI is added here once it is minted (AfricArXiv first, then Zenodo,
# Hugging Face and Software Heritage as further identifiers).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ZEDEC XERO VULPINE (ZXV): a post-quantum operating system and local multi-agent AI swarm"
abstract: >-
  ZXV is a freestanding, from-scratch C kernel with post-quantum security
  that also runs as a desktop app on macOS, Linux and Windows. It runs a
  swarm of small language models on an integer-only tensor engine that gives
  the same output bits on every CPU, under a tokens-per-cycle budget and a
  cooperative swarm economy. The same kernel builds as bare-metal UEFI discs
  for arm64 and x86_64.
authors:
